# Python bytecode from the Linux verification scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local tool/IDE/planning artifacts — not shared repo content. docs/ stays
# local except four directories and one file the repo itself depends on. Each needs the
# `/docs/*` + `!` shape, because a parent excluded with `/docs/` could not
# be re-included:
#   - agents: CLAUDE.md sends the engineering skills there for the issue
#     tracker, the triage labels and the domain docs.
#   - release-notes: release.yml refuses a tag whose
#     docs/release-notes/<version>.md is missing.
#   - superpowers/specs: shipped rustdoc links into them by URL (sirio_apply
#     alone carries nine), so an untracked spec is a 404 in published
#     documentation — and the auto-update spec those nine cite was lost
#     exactly this way. Implementation *plans* stay local on purpose: they
#     are execution scaffolding and go stale the moment the work lands.
#   - testing: the vendored Ely crate's LOCAL-CHANGES.md and the chat e2e
#     runner cite docs/testing/ely-agent-chat.md for what each check proves
#     and which platforms were seen; untracked, those would be dead links.
#   - THEME-PROVENANCE.md: CLAUDE.md, sirio_theme's presets.rs and its
#     Cargo.toml cite it as the record of where Sirio's colours come from.
/.codegraph/
/docs/*
!/docs/agents/
!/docs/release-notes/
!/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/
!/docs/testing/
!/docs/THEME-PROVENANCE.md
/output/
/plans/
